{"pair_id": "tsyn-in-contradiction-1165", "original": "The failing test asserts that a search call returns no `body` field unless the caller asks for it. After the auto-inline change, the tool attaches the body whenever a result is small, and the fixture in this test is a three-line file. I confirmed this by printing the raw response: the `body` key is present and holds all three lines. Of the possible remedies, the cheapest is to pass an explicit `include_body: false` and see whether the tool honors it. The larger-fixture option would keep the old contract intact above the size threshold. ⟦The tool never inlines a body for any result, whatever its size, so the test's original expectation was sound all along.⟧", "substituted": "The failing test asserts that a search call returns no `body` field unless the caller asks for it. After the auto-inline change, the tool attaches the body whenever a result is small, and the fixture in this test is a three-line file. I confirmed this by printing the raw response: the `body` key is present and holds all three lines. Of the possible remedies, the cheapest is to pass an explicit `include_body: false` and see whether the tool honors it. The larger-fixture option would keep the old contract intact above the size threshold. ⟦The tool still omits the body for large results, so the test's original expectation holds only above the size threshold.⟧"}
